{"type": "answer", "run_id": "chaos-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "chaos", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q13", "request_id": "chaos-20261110T183141Z-0006", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:33:01.405+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 79.966, "patience_s": 21.59, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 2454.3, "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "chaos-20261110T183141Z-0006", "question": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "The encoder network takes the raw input sequence and processes it at the fine‑grained (original) resolution before any down‑sampling occurs, while the decoder network receives the up‑sampled representations and operates again at the original resolution to reconstruct the output sequence [S2][S3].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0035", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p19-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p20-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.2 §1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0003", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p02-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b010"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.4-5 §2.1.1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0007", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p04-b013", "dynamic_chunking-p04-b014", "dynamic_chunking-p04-b015", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b001", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b002", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b003", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b004", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b009"]}], "notice": "", "eta_s": null, "model_cal